## 2. Coverage

The 54 fixtures exercise 11 distinct surface features. The AArch64 backend supports a narrow slice of the language; most fixtures test the supported slice plus adversarial fail-closed cases for shapes the backend does not support.

### 2.1 Features tested
- `println(STRING)`:  aarch64_hello, aarch64_esc, aarch64_utf8, aarch64_elseif, aarch64_if_bind_then, aarch64_iffalse_after, aarch64_if_false, aarch64_if_true, aarch64_if_nest, aarch64_outside_main (10).
- `println(INT)`:  aarch64_int, aarch64_alu_leftover, aarch64_neg, aarch64_neg_call (4).
- `println(bool)`:  aarch64_bool, aarch64_bool_bind (2).
- `println(IDENT)` from same-fn `let`:  aarch64_bind, aarch64_bool_bind, aarch64_int, aarch64_mix, aarch64_neg, aarch64_concat, aarch64_if_bind_then, aarch64_leftover_ident (8).
- `println` with mix of STRING and IDENT:  aarch64_mix, aarch64_concat (2).
- `println(STR+STR)` and `let s = STR+STR; println(s)`:  aarch64_concat (1).
- `let` (same-fn bind) for STRING, INT, true, false, -INT, call result:  aarch64_bind, aarch64_bool_bind, aarch64_int, aarch64_neg, aarch64_leftover_ident, aarch64_if_bind_then (6).
- `if true` and `if false` (const bool cond, with and without else):  aarch64_if_true, aarch64_if_false, aarch64_iffalse_after, aarch64_if_nest (4).
- `if/else-if/else` (chained):  aarch64_elseif (1).
- `if INT OP INT` for ==, !=, <, <=, >, >=, with multi-digit:  aarch64_ifeq, aarch64_ifneq, aarch64_iflt, aarch64_iflte, aarch64_ifgt, aarch64_ifgte, aarch64_if_digits (7).
- `if -INT OP INT`, `if INT OP -INT`, `if -INT OP -INT`:  aarch64_ifneg, aarch64_ifneg_rhs, aarch64_ifneg_both (3).
- `if !true` / `if !false`:  aarch64_ifnot (1).
- escape sequence inside STRING:  aarch64_esc (1).
- UTF-8 multi-byte char inside STRING:  aarch64_utf8 (1).
- adversarial fail-closed shapes (24 fixtures):  see §5.

### 2.2 Features not tested (no fixture exists)
- `struct` literal, field read, field write.
- `list` literal, list push/get/length, list index.
- `match` arm, match tag dispatch.
- `loop`, `for`, `while`, `break`, `continue`.
- float literal, float print, float compare.
- `fn` declaration with non-trivial body, function call with return value used.
- recursion (direct or indirect).
- heap, free, alloc, opt, mut, typed let, multi.
- greet fold (`println("Hello, " + name)` with hardcoded name).
- signed/unsigned distinction in compare (backend treats both as int64).
- multi-line string literal.
- escape inside an if cond (only in println).
- bitwise ops, modulo.
- string indexing, byte_at on a string.
- println of an arithmetic expression (1+2, 2*3, 10/2).
- int bind of a bool or string.

The AArch64 backend has no matcher for any of these shapes. The 54 fixtures test the 11 supported features plus the 24 fail-closed adversarial shapes listed in §5.

## 3. Untested fixtures

0 fixtures are untested. Every one of the 54 is covered by either a direct `<name>_smoke.oo` script in `ooda/scripts/` or one of the 5 bundle smoke scripts (`aarch64_if_smoke.oo`, `aarch64_if_tail_smoke.oo`, `aarch64_if_bound_smoke.oo`, `aarch64_edge_smoke.oo`, `aarch64_neg_smoke.oo`).

Coverage map (direct smokes, 37): aarch64_alu_leftover, aarch64_bind, aarch64_bool_bind, aarch64_bool, aarch64_concat, aarch64_elseif, aarch64_hello, aarch64_ifalu, aarch64_if_bind_then, aarch64_if_digits, aarch64_ifeq, aarch64_ifeq_ident, aarch64_iffalse_after, aarch64_ifgt, aarch64_ifgt_and, aarch64_ifgt_ident, aarch64_ifgt_lhs_ident, aarch64_ifgte, aarch64_ifgte_ident, aarch64_iflte, aarch64_iflte_ident, aarch64_iflt, aarch64_iflt_rhs_ident, aarch64_ifneg, aarch64_ifneg_both, aarch64_ifneg_ident, aarch64_ifneg_rhs, aarch64_ifneg_rhs_ident, aarch64_ifneq, aarch64_if_nest, aarch64_ifnot, aarch64_ifnot_ident, aarch64_ifparen, aarch64_int, aarch64_leftover_ident, aarch64_mix, aarch64_neg.

Coverage map (bundle smokes, 17):
- `aarch64_edge_smoke.oo`: aarch64_empty, aarch64_esc, aarch64_multi, aarch64_nomain, aarch64_outside_main, aarch64_utf8 (6).
- `aarch64_if_bound_smoke.oo`: aarch64_if_eq00, aarch64_if_lte010, aarch64_iflt_ident, aarch64_if_ovf (4).
- `aarch64_if_smoke.oo`: aarch64_if_false, aarch64_if_ident, aarch64_if_true (3).
- `aarch64_if_tail_smoke.oo`: aarch64_if_eqeqeq, aarch64_if_true_and, aarch64_if_true_eq (3).
- `aarch64_neg_smoke.oo`: aarch64_neg_call (1).

Verified 2026-08-25: `grep -l <fixture> ooda/scripts/aarch64_*_smoke.oo` returns at least one match for every one of the 54 fixtures.

## 4. Misfiled fixtures

1 fixture is misfiled.

| Current path | Suggested path | Why |
|---|---|---|
| `ooda/fixtures/aarch64_empty.oo` | `ooda/fixtures-aarch64/aarch64_empty.oo` | 0 bytes, 0 lines, no `pub fn main`, no body. Listed in the 54 because the filename starts with `aarch64_`, but it is not a real fixture: the Academy header the other 53 carry is absent (the file is empty). The aarch64 backend should refuse it (`aarch64_emit.oo:116` "need fn main" + `aarch64_emit.oo:128` "empty"); the smoke bundle `aarch64_edge_smoke.oo:71` already exercises this case. Move it with the other 53 when Tier 4 ships, but flag it in the run-probe so the empty-file smoke is not counted as a fixture green-light. |

Note: the deep-dive (`aarch64-deep-dive.oot:58`, Turn 4 at lines 113-117) already calls all 54 misfiled at the directory level (in `fixtures/` instead of `fixtures-aarch64/`). The 1 above is the structural outlier inside that set: the only file with no source content.

## 5. Aspirational fixtures

24 fixtures test shapes the AArch64 backend does NOT support today. They are fail-closed tests; the smoke scripts assert that the emit either ERRs leftover or refuses to write `_start`.

| Fixture | What it tests | AArch64 feature it expects to compile |
|---|---|---|
| `aarch64_alu_leftover.oo` | println(1+2) | ALU fold inside println (int op int) |
| `aarch64_ifalu.oo` | if 1+2==3 | ALU in if cond |
| `aarch64_if_eq00.oo` | if 00==0 | leading-zero INT canonicalization in cond |
| `aarch64_if_eqeqeq.oo` | if 1==1==0 | chained EQEQ after INT==INT |
| `aarch64_ifeq_ident.oo` | if x==1 | IDENT on lhs of INT==INT |
| `aarch64_ifgt_and.oo` | if 1>2 && true | ANDAND tail after folded INT compare |
| `aarch64_ifgte_ident.oo` | if x>=1 | IDENT on lhs of INT>=INT |
| `aarch64_ifgt_ident.oo` | if 1>x | IDENT on rhs of INT>INT |
| `aarch64_ifgt_lhs_ident.oo` | if x>1 | IDENT on lhs of INT>INT |
| `aarch64_if_ident.oo` | if x | bare IDENT in cond (no compare) |
| `aarch64_if_lte010.oo` | if 10<=010 | leading-zero INT on rhs of order compare |
| `aarch64_iflte_ident.oo` | if 1<=x | IDENT on rhs of INT<=INT |
| `aarch64_iflt_ident.oo` | if x<2 | IDENT on lhs of INT<INT |
| `aarch64_iflt_rhs_ident.oo` | if 1<x | IDENT on rhs of INT<INT |
| `aarch64_ifneg_ident.oo` | if -x<1 | MINUS IDENT in cond |
| `aarch64_ifneg_rhs_ident.oo` | if 1>-x | INT OP MINUS IDENT in cond |
| `aarch64_ifnot_ident.oo` | if !x | BANG IDENT in cond |
| `aarch64_if_ovf.oo` | if 9223372036854775808<1 | INT above signed 64-bit max |
| `aarch64_ifparen.oo` | if (true) | LPAREN before KW_TRUE in cond |
| `aarch64_if_true_and.oo` | if true && false | ANDAND tail after KW_TRUE |
| `aarch64_if_true_eq.oo` | if true==false | EQEQ tail after KW_TRUE |
| `aarch64_leftover_ident.oo` | let x = foo(); println(x) | call-result IDENT in println |
| `aarch64_neg_call.oo` | println(-foo()) | MINUS call in println |
| `aarch64_outside_main.oo` | println in helper + main | println outside main scope |

Two more fixtures are broken in a different way (no main at all): `aarch64_nomain.oo` (helper only) and `aarch64_empty.oo` (0 bytes). Both expect the same ERR path (`aarch64_emit.oo:116`). They are listed under §1 and §4 but not counted as aspirational feature coverage.

Every aspirational fixture is paired with a smoke that asserts the fail-closed behavior. Static evidence: `aarch64_emit.oo:104`, `:107`, `:120` set `leftover = true`; `:121` exits 1. None of the 24 expect the AArch64 backend to compile them.
